On 2007-11-14, Kent Paul Dolan wrote:
> YANI: We could just put the death threat back into
> pudding farming, as a "fix".
>
> [puddings occasionally split into nasties]
>
> A 0.5% chance of getting some selection of two of
> the most difficult monsters which can currently be
> generated, instead of child puddings with nearly no
> HPs, would make pudding farming a thing one did for
> limited periods and at substantial risk, to balance
> the potential death drop and sacrifice fodder
> rewards of pudding farming.

This would eliminate farming completely for weak characters, and make it
only slightly more intersting for tougher ones who don't have much of a
problem dealing with high difficulty monsters. For those, the reward is
still infinite. If you only chose from monsters eligible for random
generation, to keep it open for weaker characters, then all you need to
survive those is a little extra equipment, like wished-for DSM in the early
game which gives you an AC so good that randomly generated monsters aren't
a problem.

I'd say there's no way around diminishing returns to fix pudding farming.
I don't say the expected profit should be zero, or even small, since it
does require some patience, but it needs to be adapted.

